  "solution": {
    "text": "In <math><mo>(</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mo>(</mo><mtext>b</mtext><mo>)</mo></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>d</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo></math> Sulphur, nitrogen and Mn are in their maximum oxidation state, so they can only be reduced and thus can act only as oxidising agent.<br /><br /><math><mo>(</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>)</mo></math> only <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> will act as both.<br /><br />(i) In case of oxidising agent<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> itself get reduced:<br /><br />e.g.,<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0037_0ebbe3291c52.png\" style=\"width: 172px; height: 40px;\" /><br /><br />(ii) In case of reducing agent <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> itself get oxidise<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0037_023c6da1ed69.png\" style=\"width: 129px; height: 39px;\" />"
